      "plaintextBody": "AWS Health Event\n\nImportant notice about your AWS Account regarding VPN connections [AWS Account: 090594843435, VPN Connection: vpn-0e3b691c8a991d18e, Tunnel Outside IP: 13.56.36.146]\n\n [Effective December 1, 2026, the affected resources associated with this AWS Health event type will be provided in the ARN format arn:aws:ec2:us-west-1:090594843435:vpn-connection/vpn-0e3b691c8a991d18e. Please review and update any Amazon EventBridge rules and/or other integrations which reference these affected resources values before December 1, 2026.]\n\nHello,\n\nYou are receiving this message because your VPN Connection vpn-0e3b691c8a991d18e in the us-west-1 Region had a momentary lapse of redundancy as one of two tunnel endpoints (Tunnel Outside IP: 13.56.36.146) was replaced. Connectivity on the second tunnel was not affected during this time. Both tunnels are now operating normally.\n\nReplacements can occur for several reasons, and be initiated either by AWS or when you modify your VPN Connection [1]. AWS-initiated replacement reasons include health, software upgrades, and when underlying hardware is retired.\n\nThis replacement was AWS Initiated.\n\nAWS Site-to-Site VPN includes two tunnels so that you can maintain a highly available VPN connection. If you have configured your VPN Customer Gateway to use both tunnels, then your VPN Connection will have utilized the alternate tunnel during the replacement process. For more on tunnel endpoint replacements, please see our documentation (2). If you have not configured your VPN Customer Gateway to use both tunnels, then your VPN Connection may have been interrupted during the replacement. We encourage you to configure your router to use both tunnels. You can obtain the VPN Connection configuration recommendations for several types of VPN devices from the AWS Management Console [3]. On the \"Amazon VPC\" tab, select \"VPN Connections\". Then highlight the VPN Connection and choose \"Download Configuration\".\n\n[1] https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/endpoint-replacements.html\n[2] https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/monitoring-vpn-health-events.html\n[3] https://console.aws.amazon.com\n\n.\n\n==================\nView in Notification Center\nhttps://console.aws.amazon.com/notifications/home#/notifications/AWS-Health/Operations/a01m0wv6b8tey1fap8zqp3fqfgm/details\n\nView details in service console\nhttps://health.aws.amazon.com/health/home?region=us-west-1#/event-log?eventID=arn:aws:health:us-west-1::event/VPN/AWS_VPN_REDUNDANCY_LOSS/AWS_VPN_REDUNDANCY_LOSS-1787674395278-13-56-36-146-US-WEST-1&eventTab�tails&layout=vertical\n\n==================\n\nMessage metadata\n\nAffected account: 090594843435\n\nEvent type code: AWS_VPN_REDUNDANCY_LOSS\n\nEvent region: us-west-1\n\nService: VPN\n\nEvent type category: accountNotification\n\nStart time: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:10:31 GMT\n\n==================\nAWS managed notification details\nAWS Health: Operations events notifications are generated by AWS and sent to selected account contacts. You can add additional delivery channels for these notifications using AWS managed notifications subscriptions (https://us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com/notifications/home#/managed-notifications).\n\nEvent type: AWS Health Event\n\nCategory: Operations\n\n==================\nThank you,\nAmazon Web Services\n\n==================\nYou are receiving this email because eng@pws.bz is subscribed to AWS Health: Operations events notifications (https://console.aws.amazon.com/notifications/home#/managed-notifications/category/AWS-Health/sub-category/Operations/details). If you do not wish to receive emails for these AWS managed notifications, you may unsubscribe (https://us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com/notifications/home#/managed-notifications). If you believe you've received this email by error or are experiencing issues managing email subscription, please contact us (https://aws.amazon.com/contact-us/).\n\nAmazon Web Services